# Enterprise Route Architecture: Duplication & Concurrency

This document outlines the architectural changes required to bring UPBus to enterprise-level scalability, addressing Route Data Duplication and Concurrency exactly as requested (based on the GSRTC model).

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **PostGIS Requirement:** The plan includes converting stop coordinates to PostGIS geometry and using `ST_DWithin` for spatial anti-duplication. This requires the PostgreSQL database to have the PostGIS extension installed. 
> 
> **Redis / Kafka Requirement:** For the Live Tracking Concurrency (Scenario C), the plan introduces Redis Streams (or Kafka). We will use Redis Streams as it's typically easier to set up alongside a standard Node.js backend. 

