### Backend Logic & Algorithms
We will introduce new services and algorithms to enforce the new schema constraints.

#### [NEW] [frechetDistance.ts](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/engine/frechetDistance.ts)
- Implement the **Discrete Fréchet Distance** algorithm.
- This will be used as a cleanup cron job/utility to detect parallel routes (within 200m) and merge them into a single master segment ID.

#### [NEW] [routeManager.ts](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/services/routeManager.ts)
- Implement **MVCC (Multi-Version Concurrency Control)** for Route Edits.
- When an admin updates a route, it creates a V2 clone in the database.
- A midnight cron job deprecates V1 and makes V2 active.

#### [MODIFY] [tripService.ts](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/services/tripService.ts)
- Implement **Optimistic Locking** for trip assignments.
- SQL queries will explicitly include `WHERE id = $1 AND version_number = $2`. If `rowCount === 0`, it rejects the assignment (preventing race conditions).

#### [NEW] [gpsIngestionQueue.ts](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/services/gpsIngestionQueue.ts)
- Replace direct DB inserts with a **Redis Stream** (or Kafka) publisher/consumer model.
- Pings are published to the stream using `vehicle_id` as the partition key.
- A consumer processes messages strictly in chronological order, discarding older timestamps if a newer one was already processed.

